{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 5, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a nobleman and leader of the County of Tripoli from 1152 to 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. *Early Life* Raymond III was born around 1140 and was still a minor when his father was assassinated in 1152. His mother Hodierna acted as regent until he came of age. Raymond III was known to be a capable and intelligent leader.\n\nAs Count of Tripoli Raymond III was involved in various conflicts with neighboring states and the Zengid dynasty. In 1160 he was taken captive by Nur ad-Din Zangi and held for nine years until he was ransomed in 1164. *Imprisonment and Ransom* During his imprisonment his stepbrother Bohemond III of Antioch acted as regent of Tripoli. After his release Raymond III played a significant role in the politics of the Crusader states.\n\nIn 1174 Raymond III was appointed regent of the Kingdom of Jerusalem for King Baldwin IV who was suffering from leprosy. *Regency* As regent Raymond III worked to secure the kingdom's borders and prevent the rise of Saladin. However his regency was marked by power struggles with other nobles and the influence of the Latin Patriarch of Jerusalem. Raymond III's regency ended in 1176 when Baldwin IV came of age.\n\nRaymond III's later years were marked by conflict with the Knights Templar and the rise of Saladin. He was one of the leaders of the Crusader army at the Battle of Hattin in 1187 where they were defeated by Saladin. After the battle Raymond III escaped to Tripoli and later died in 1187. He was succeeded by his godson Raymond IV who was the son of Bohemond III of Antioch. Raymond III's legacy was complex and multifaceted and he remains one of the most important figures in the history of the Crusader states. He was known for his intelligence and military prowess but also for his involvement in the power struggles that plagued the Crusader states.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.011065074242651463}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": " III", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.0003358753747306764}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0016014858847483993}, {"token": " nob", "logprob": -0.1395372599363327}, {"token": "leman", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -0.03762337192893028}, {"token": " leader", "logprob": -1.2146894931793213}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.06197960302233696}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " County", "logprob": -0.16057026386260986}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " from", "logprob": -0.9760180711746216}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -7.152555099310121e-07}, {"token": "115", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": " to", "logprob": -1.6927575416048057e-05}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": "118", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "7", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -4.172316494077677e-06}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.0003522014303598553}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.0003401654539629817}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.3787054717540741}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -1.311301275563892e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -0.00043156370520591736}, {"token": " II", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -5.125986263010418e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " and", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": " Hod", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": "ierna", "logprob": -5.960462772